factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 6 problems
  The reel_script says the incident took place in Jothi Nagar 'D' Colony, but the article only says Jothi Nagar 'D' Colony is where Rajagopal and Prabhu are from; the article does not state the stabbing happened there (it gives only 'Pollachi area').
  The reel_script and caption say Srinivasan stabbed Rajagopal and his driver, and the caption says 'ராஜகோபால் மற்றும் அவரது ஓட்டுநர் அப்துல் முனாப்' were stabbed; the article supports this, but the slide 'என்ன நடந்தது?' says the incident happened 'பொள்ளாச்சி ஜோதிநகர், 'டி' காலனியில் சம்பவம்', which is an unsupported location claim, as noted above.
  The reel_script states Rajagopal's son Prabhu had the money dispute, but the article says the dispute was between Prabhu and Srinivasan and then describes Rajagopal and the driver as the stabbed persons; the reel_script omits that the dispute was described as 'கூறப்படுகிறது' (alleged), which is a mixing of claims presented as fact.
  The reel_script omits that the stabbing was reported by police to have happened in the course of a dispute 'on the day before' (நேற்று) - it does include this, so no issue; however the caption says 'அப்துல் முனாப் (44 வயது), ஆகிய இருவரையும்' which is a garbled Tamil sentence with a misplaced comma and a grammatically broken clause ('ராஜகோபால்... ஆகிய இருவரையும் சீனிவாசன்... கத்தியால் குத்தியதாக'), making its meaning unclear.
  The caption's 'நடவடிக்கை: இரு தரப்பு புகார்களின் பேரில் போலீசார் விசாரணை' describes the action as a result, but the article says only that an inquiry is underway; no arrest is mentioned, and the draft does not claim one, so this is acceptable.
  The reel_script calls Abdul Munaf the 'ஓட்டுநர்' (driver) of Rajagopal, which the article states, but the slide labels him 'ராஜகோபாலின் ஓட்டுநர்' - consistent. No issue there.
